- action(n1, "start"): Hallucinates a step not documented; the description states the process "starts with receiving a request for information," so no prior action should exist.
- action(n5, "end process"): Hallucinates a final step not documented; the description simply concludes with "the process comes to an end," which should map directly to an end node rather than an intermediate action.
- actor(a_default, "Default", [...]): Misrepresents responsibility assignment; the source explicitly attributes the process to the "referee," but the model assigns all nodes to a generic "Default" actor instead of the specified role.